DTEND:20261213T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261213T190000Z
UID:Kg6YB4Gxet
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 103 mins (1h43m)\n\nCommunity Screenings  Holiday F
 avorites Hollywood’s troubled transition from silent to talking pictures
  at the end of the 1920s provided the inspiration for perhaps the greatest
  of movie musicals\, starring Gene Kelly\, Debbie Reynolds\, and Donald O
 ’Connor.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/community-screening
 s/singin-in-the-rain-cs\n\nEstimated start: 11:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jawbreaker: A Film About Anti Cimex
DTSTART:20261214T031500Z
DTEND:20261214T055500Z
DTSTAMP:20261214T031500Z
UID:Zuls6bhO6r
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 145 mins (2h25m)\n\nPresented by Exploited Partisan
 s. Jawbreaker depicts Anti Cimex – the band that shaped Scandinavian ha
 rdcore punk and became one of Sweden's most influential musical exports.T
 hrough archive material\, international perspectives\, and a dreamy\, hum
 orous tone\, directors Tomas Haglund and Oskar Sjödin paint a portrait o
 f a musical legacy that still packs a punch.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinem
 a/in-theaters/jawbreaker-a-film-about-anti-cimex\n\nEstimated start: 19:30
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
